        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mel Brooks, Alan Johnson, Charles Durning\n- Films: To Be or Not to Be, The Sting, Dog Day Afternoon, The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas, Tootsie\n- Topics: American war comedy films, acting careers\n\nFacts:\n- Mel Brooks was born as Melvin Kaminsky on June 28, 1926, and he is an American actor, writer, producer, director, comedian, and composer.\n- Charles Durning's best-known film roles included The Sting in 1973 and Dog Day Afternoon in 1975.\n- Charles Durning's best-known comedy film roles included The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas in 1982, Tootsie in 1982, and To Be or Not to Be in 1983.\n- To Be or Not to Be is a 1983 American war comedy film directed by Alan Johnson and produced by Mel Brooks.",
